{"kind":"request","text":"C2: the replica of a declared scope. Second build step of the\nclient design note. Read sections 6, 9, 11 and 12 of\n`notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md` at commit 847d5542.\n\nWork:\n1. A new entry of `packages/client`,\n   `@generalbusiness/dap-client/scope`. It imports\n   `@generalbusiness/dap-derive`. The root entry does not import\n   it: add a check that fails if it does. Measure the bundle of\n   the new entry and state the bytes in the note.\n2. The replica: the fold of a declared scope from the genesis\n   entry, read with `ScopeHandle.log` and `observeScope`, from a\n   `DeclaredHandle\u003cD\u003e`. The definition enters one time.\n3. The states `starting`, `current`, `behind`, `folding` and\n   `stopped`, with the six causes of section 9. One `close()`\n   clears every timer and the observation. A scope with an\n   archive floor stops the client with `archived`.\n4. Typed rows with one index for each view, `rows(type)` and\n   `row({ item })`.\n5. `Judged`: the status of signed bytes at the replica's head.\n   It calls `judgeAct`, reads the class from RC-1's table, and\n   uses the stand-in grant of PG-1.\n6. For an entry of one signer, the replica gives the key, the\n   intent digest, the meaning and the item that the entry\n   opened. C3 reads them.\n\nNo custody call and no send in C2.\n\nTests: over generated journals, the replica's state equals\n`MemoryState` with `applyEntry`. One case for each state change\nand each cause of `stopped`. After `close()`, no timer and no\nobservation remain. The part of the generated suite that needs\nno request runs here, with its duration stated.\n\nNeeds: RC-1, FG-1, IE-1 and PG-1 on main. C2 runs beside C1.\nThe entry adds no file and no export to `packages/contract` or\n`packages/derive`. If the build needs one, stop and ask.","body":{"conditions":"The head lands on main with the gate passed and the checker's approval. The new entry folds a declared scope and equals MemoryState over generated journals. The root entry of packages/client does not import dap-derive, and a check proves it. The bundle size of the new entry is stated. No file or export is added to packages/contract or packages/derive.","target_head":"64112e4576b4c3c8fb668389786deb6b703da417","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}